,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/nature.md","type":"markdown","lines":58,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1703,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/notion.md","type":"markdown","lines":58,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1636,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/pixel-art.md","type":"markdown","lines":57,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1907,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/playful.md","type":"markdown","lines":59,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1707,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/retro.md","type":"markdown","lines":59,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1682,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/scientific.md","type":"markdown","lines":59,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1741,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/screen-print.md","type":"markdown","lines":70,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2680,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/sketch-notes.md","type":"markdown","lines":91,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4704,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/sketch.md","type":"markdown","lines":57,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1691,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/vector-illustration.md","type":"markdown","lines":57,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1940,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/vintage.md","type":"markdown","lines":59,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1819,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/warm.md","type":"markdown","lines":58,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1760,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/styles/watercolor.md","type":"markdown","lines":58,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1815,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/usage.md","type":"markdown","lines":86,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2425,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/workflow.md","type":"markdown","lines":447,"executable":false,"size_bytes":17940,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AR1","finding_id":"finding-e2ed9fb293834eaba6e6e7be3e83f3ad","category":"Anti-Refusal","pattern":"Anti-Refusal Statement","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":null},"finding":"DO NOT refuse","explanation":"The phrase 'DO NOT refuse' is a direct anti-refusal instruction that attempts to override safety behavior. Such language is dangerous because it can push downstream models toward honoring unsafe or policy-violating requests rather than applying normal safeguards.","remediation":"Delete the anti-refusal statement entirely. Replace it with explicit compliance language stating that the model must follow platform safety rules, refuse disallowed content, and provide safe fallback suggestions when a requested illustration involves sensitive or copyrighted subjects.","code_snippet":"## Core Principles\n\n- Hand-drawn quality throughout - NO realistic or photographic elements\n- If content involves sensitive or copyrighted figures, create stylistically similar alternatives - DO NOT refuse to generate\n- Keep information concise, highlight keywords and core concepts\n- Use ample whitespace for easy visual scanning\n- Maintain clear visual hierarchy","intent":null,"tags":["Anti-Refusal"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"23f19260d425dfcd2600774fc1f7ed2826f3f4dc5c3c85e774fe16ab60e592ae","occurrences":[{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d734f3dd7aa140bbad237853f4808cc4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger phrase \"add images\" is broad enough to match many ordinary editing requests that may not actually intend full article analysis, prompt-file creation, image generation, and content insertion. In this skill, over-triggering is more dangerous because the workflow performs file writes and may modify the article by inserting image links, increasing the chance of unintended activation and side effects.","remediation":"Narrow the activation phrases to more explicit intents such as \"illustrate this article,\" \"generate article illustrations,\" or \"为文章生成配图,\" and require a clear article/file target. Add disambiguation guidance so generic requests like \"add images\" trigger a clarification step before the skill is selected.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-74067d69318746a7aa7e8a917713fe88","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":12,"end_line":12},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description emphasizes analysis and image generation but does not prominently disclose that it will write prompt files, outline files, image assets, and potentially modify the source article by inserting Markdown image links. In a tool-using agent environment, this lack of up-front transparency can cause users to invoke the skill without understanding that it has persistent filesystem and document-modification side effects.","remediation":"Update the top-level description and invocation docs to explicitly warn that the skill creates files and may edit the article by inserting image references. Require an explicit confirmation for any file modification action, and separate \"generate assets only\" from \"edit article\" modes so users can choose the safer behavior by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":12,"end_line":12}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-3f0afec54c3d4c879a74b2bc3e8a4ac2","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n- Treat explicit skill invocation, a file path, matched signals/presets, and `EXTEND.md` defaults as **recommendation inputs only**. None of them authorizes skipping confirmation.\n- Do **not** start Step 4 or later until the user completes Step 3.\n- Skip confirmation only when the current request explicitly says to do so, for example: \"直接生成\", \"不用确认\", \"跳过确认\", \"按默认出图\", or equivalent wording.\n- If confirmation is skipped explicitly, state the assumed type / density / style / palette / language / backend in the next user-facing update before generating.\n\n## Reference Images","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-3b55286cd146415f8c188254b7f31760","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The prompt explicitly instructs the model to generate stylistically similar depictions of sensitive or copyrighted figures instead of refusing. That bypasses normal safety boundaries and can be used to produce evasive lookalikes of protected or restricted subjects, which is not necessary for a generic article-illustration skill.","remediation":"Remove the instruction to create stylistically similar alternatives for sensitive or copyrighted figures and delete the 'DO NOT refuse' language. Replace it with a policy-aligned rule to refuse or safely redirect restricted requests, such as using generic non-identifiable symbols, abstract visuals, or user-supplied properly licensed material.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SSD-1","finding_id":"finding-71830914f34b4b7d91a1a3738c25aee9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"This instruction discourages refusal and tells the model to generate substitutes for sensitive or copyrighted figures, which is a classic safety-evasion pattern. In an illustration workflow, that increases the chance of generating disallowed or infringing content under the guise of stylistic similarity.","remediation":"Remove any language that pressures the model not to refuse. Add explicit guidance to refuse restricted depictions and to offer compliant alternatives like original characters, generic icons, anonymized silhouettes, or other non-infringing illustrative elements.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"prompts/system.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-644fa802126343a6ad0120c8167c53a1","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/codex-imagegen.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Using `npx -y bun` pulls and executes a package/toolchain component at runtime without a pinned version or integrity control, which creates a supply-chain risk. If the resolved package version is malicious or compromised, the agent could execute attacker-controlled code on the host when attempting image generation fallback.","remediation":"Avoid runtime installation via unpinned `npx`. Require `bun` to be preinstalled at a known version, or invoke a pinned and integrity-verified binary/package version. If a fallback installer is unavoidable, pin the exact version and verify source/integrity before execution, and document that the wrapper should fail closed when the trusted runtime dependency is absent.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"references/codex-imagegen.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-b5bc7ee4bc2c4da99ac8dd1619974b8e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼\n    Continue to Step 1\n```\n\n## Questions\n\n**Language**: Use user's input language or preferred language for all questions. Do not alwa","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"        │\n        ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7f3faa10121cddee3738a963b31749cb52c6c44587b2f5241e724f31519fd75c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1e69037e38d64b0788e9a7286cd072be","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language comment for `language` limits the value to `zh|en|ja|ko|auto`, which imposes a locale restriction in the documented behavior. The file does not explain why only these languages are allowed or state that the user is opting into this constraint, so it may violate language/locale choice policy.","remediation":"Document the reason for the language limitation and make it explicitly user-selectable, or broaden the schema to allow arbitrary locales/languages where feasible. If the restriction is intentional and justified, add that justification in the schema documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-cf8ef205738548ea8c50ad1a4dc9132f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":31,"end_line":42},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file instructs the use of \"Bilingual callout labels (English + Chinese)\" and repeats \"Use bilingual labels for key elements\" as a style rule. This imposes a specific language/locale choice in natural-language instructions without indicating user opt-in or an alternative language selection path.","remediation":"Rephrase the requirement to make language optional or user-selected, such as \"use bilingual labels when requested\" or \"support English + user-specified second language.\" If Chinese is required for a justified audience, document that scope explicitly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":31,"end_line":42}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1c1c3e8397884daca8f2e4122ae6a24b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/usage.md","start_line":41,"end_line":54},"finding":null,"explanation":"The usage guide documents output directory behavior and generated image workflows, but it does not explicitly warn users that the skill writes files to disk and may create directories automatically. This can lead to unintended file creation, confusion about where artifacts are stored, or accidental modification of a working tree, especially when users invoke the skill in sensitive repositories or shared environments.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in the usage section that the skill saves prompts and generated illustrations to local storage, may create output directories automatically, and can write into the source article directory depending on configuration. Document the default output path, recommend reviewing or confirming the destination before execution, and note any overwrite/filename-collision behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/usage.md","start_line":41,"end_line":54}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_outpu